{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773924051,"nonce":"I4tkznPv7PWT/deXdrrjfQPiJMk=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM70dsdh","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/9","origin":"github"},"title":"Migrate WiFi from dedicated links to shared APs with roaming (Option A → B)","message":"## Summary\n\nMigrate the shore-side WiFi architecture from dedicated point-to-point links (Option A) to shared access points with automatic roaming (Option B), so both IzzyBoat and BizzyBoat can connect to either shore antenna without manual re-aiming.\n\nPart of #5\n\n## Current State (Option A)\n\nEach boat has a dedicated WiFi link:\n- Shore: MikroTik SXTsq Lite5 (one per boat, directional, pointed at different areas)\n- Boat: MikroTik OmniTIK 5 ac (omnidirectional)\n- Protocol: Nv2 (MikroTik proprietary TDMA)\n- Separate SSIDs, separate channels, separate subnets\n\n## Target State (Option B)\n\nBoth shore SXTsqs act as APs on the same SSID. Boat OmniTIKs auto-roam to the strongest signal.\n\n### Required Changes\n\n1. **License upgrade**: Both shore SXTsqs from Level 3 → Level 4 ($45 each) to unlock `ap-bridge` mode (multi-client)\n2. **Protocol switch**: Nv2 → standard 802.11ac (Nv2 does not support background scanning or roaming)\n3. **SSID unification**: Same SSID, same auth, same channel on both shore APs\n4. **Firmware alignment**: All four radios on matching RouterOS 7.x (IzzyBoat currently has a v6/v7 mismatch between shore and boat radios)\n\n### How Roaming Works\n\n- OmniTIK in station mode periodically background-scans for APs with matching SSID\n- Scan interval adapts: more aggressive as signal degrades, less frequent when signal is strong\n- When a stronger AP is found, the client roams automatically\n- Operational benefit: deploy at pier (connects to pier antenna) → transit to test area → auto-roams to test-area antenna. No manual re-aiming needed.\n\n### Trade-offs (Nv2 → 802.11ac)\n\n| Aspect | Nv2 | 802.11ac |\n|---|---|---|\n| Roaming | Not supported | Background scan + auto-roam |\n| Throughput | Higher (TDMA) | Standard (CSMA/CA) |\n| Latency | Lower | Slightly higher |\n| Multi-client | Yes | Yes |\n\nThroughput/latency differences are negligible for the UDP bridge data rates (~1.5 MB/s).\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- BizzyBoat Option A WiFi link operational and stable\n- Both SXTsq Level 4 licenses purchased\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- [ ] Purchase Level 4 license upgrades for both SXTsqs\n- [ ] Flash all four radios to same RouterOS 7.x release\n- [ ] Configure both SXTsqs as `ap-bridge`, same SSID/channel/auth\n- [ ] Configure OmniTIKs as `station-bridge` with 802.11ac\n- [ ] Test single-boat roaming: deploy → transit → verify auto-handoff\n- [ ] Test dual-boat: both boats connected to same AP, then one roams\n- [ ] Verify UDP bridge seamless failover during roam events\n- [ ] Measure roam time and any data gaps\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6`","files":null}]}